9. Underlines that unilateral coercive measures should not impede the delivery of humanitarian assistance, recovery and reconstruction, in accordance with international law;

10. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to report to the Council on the situation in Syria, including the implementation of this resolution, humanitarian access, the political process, attacks on civilians, medical facilities and schools, and any use of chemical weapons, within 30 days;

11. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

